「…我已经说过了，\n还有你这必杀的一张牌啊？」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dI do. To tell the truth, I've already put it in motion.\d%K%P
「那当然了。\n倒不如说，其实他已经同意了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh...?\d%K%P
「哎…？」%K%P
Considering how I wasn't expecting a reply, I found myself\nmomentarily taken by surprise, and ultimately mustered\nonly an awkward grunt in response.%K%P
本来只准备当做耳边风一般来应答的，\n但姬绪小姐在这个绝妙的时机发言，\n让我发出了惊喜的声音。%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dI've already made a deal with Mr. Hiragi. He's gonna\nsupport us unconditionally during today's meeting. ...I\nthink we've already won.\d%K%P
「我和平木先生缔结了密约呢。\n他对今天的动员大会，表示全力支持。\n…这就算是赢了吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dW-Wait a second! I've asked him countless times, only to\nbe turned down!\d%K%P
「喂、喂等一下啊！\n我低声下气地求了他这么多次，都不见他同意啊？」%K%P
Maybe I was letting it get to my head, but I was pretty\nsure Chief Hiragi would be more inclined to support me\nrather than listen to Himeo's orders...%K%P
这么说虽然有些自吹自擂的感觉吧，\n但我一直觉得，平木副部长，比起姫绪小姐的命令，\n他应当优先选择听取我的…%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dYou're right. I'm confident you're the only one who\ncould've moved him.\d%K%P
「是呢。\n大概，除了你以外，\n没人能把他说动吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dB-But didn't you just say...\d%K%P
「但、但是，姫绪小姐…」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dThat's why I told him I would return my secretary to the\naccounting department, provided all of this went well.\d%K%P
「所以我是这么说的啊…\n『这次的工作如果顺利的话，我就让秘书回到会计部』\n就是这样」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh...?\d%K%P
「诶…？」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dHe really wanted you.\nHe even made me sign a contract on the spot. Look.\d%K%P
「看来他很想要你呢。\n甚至在当场签了契约书呢。\n你看」%K%P
The paper she dangled in front of me had two signatures on\nit -- one belonging to Himeo, and another to our Vice\nChief.%K%P
姫绪小姐拿出的一份纸张，\n上面确实有她的印章，副部长的印章，\n一起盖在了上面。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWhat is the... meaning of this?\d%K%P
「这是…怎么回事儿？」%K%P
The letters -- undoubtedly penned by her -- spelled out\n\dYoshimura Osamu will be transferred to the department of\naccounting on January 1st, 200X.\d%K%P
文面上，她的笔迹白纸黑字，\n『２００×年１月１日签订，将芳村理交给会计部』\n毫无疑义地写明着。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dDoes that mean that I'm getting relieved as your\nsecretary?\d%K%P
「我…要从你的秘书岗位上离任了吗？」%K%P
It was something I had sincerely hoped for last September.\nThe accounting department was where I could utilize most\nof my experience -- the place I found the most comfortable\nworking at.%K%P
事实上，９月上旬我就是这么希望的吧。\n那是和我的经验与知识最匹配、最合适的安排。%K%P
Had my life not been turned around by this very woman\nstanding in front of me, I would've accepted the offer\nwith open arms.%K%P
我眼前的女性，将我的人生峰回路转，\n却毫不犹豫地签下了那封简短的辞令，明白无误…%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dThank you for everything. This will be our final job as a\nteam.\d%K%P
